rom the start or do you unlock things  throughout the story like should you  play the story before you get into  making no I wouldn't say so you do there  are some things you can unlock by  beating the story it's just a few I  think only if I remember correctly it's  either just one or two items that you  can use in the maker toolset but they're  not hugely impactful not like the sort  of additions that intended  has made otherwise so I would say if you  want to make stages go right in if you  need a break  the Stormlands a great place to just  play some fun levels well speaking of  making stages one another new addition  is Yama Mors dojo which apparently is  pretty in-depth teaching new players how  to create their own stages yeah if I  remember correctly I think Yamamura was  present in the 3ds version had sort of  like a light tutorial system but here  there's like a series of courses not  like Mario courses but like study  courses you can do to become a  thoughtful capable creator and it does  start off pretty simple right like  here's how you achieve certain  objectives when it comes to practically  building a level but then it gets into  sort of like philosophical things like  what is your mindset when you go to  build a level like how do you approach  the broad concept and you know whittled  down to the the individual things you  want to focus on it's pretty cool now  respect and there's a funny little  banter between the pigeon and Nina I  think her name is the female character  who's like the budding Mario maker  standing in for you it's definitely  helpful yeah what about the actual  interface itself you can build stages  docked and I feel like that experience  could be vastly different considering  one you can actually use your finger or  stylus to yes if you have a stylus  making on the switch itself and handheld  mode is the most ideal way to do it  without a stylus you're gonna run into  some clumsy things here there like at  first it didn't bother me